WL1283 instrumentation, Linux 7.3.3 — archived at session 37 (absolute).

This patch re-adds the WL1283-specific code that was removed from the active
tree and from 0001-playbook-winchester-7.3.3.patch under DECISIONS §46 and
HANDOFF §0c.  It applies to the *clean* base tree (the tree produced by the
current 0001-playbook-winchester-7.3.3.patch) with `patch -p1`.

Contents (all WL1283-specific):
  * drivers/mmc/host/omap_hsmmc.c
      - pb_init_hz (MMC5 init-clock override) module parameter + calc_divisor
      - PBCLK / PBD command/register tracing
      - pb_sdio_ocr_quirk + the 480d5000 MMC_CAP2_SDIO_OCR_PROBE_FFFF00 select
      - pb_enable_fref_clk2() and pb_wl1283_reset_pulse() (already unused)
      - the 480d5000 PBGPIO one-shot dump in probe
  * drivers/mmc/core/core.c   — PBCMD (480d5000 CMD trace) and PBVOLT
  * drivers/mmc/core/mmc_ops.c — PBOCR
  * drivers/mmc/core/sdio.c    — the CMD5 arg 0x00ffff00 probe quirk
  * include/linux/mmc/host.h   — MMC_CAP2_SDIO_OCR_PROBE_FFFF00
  * arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-winchester.dts
      - vwl1283 regulator, sdmmc5_pins, fref_clk2_out_pins, fref_clk_pins,
        wl1283_ctrl_pins, wl1283-en-hog, and the &mmc5 host

This is the state that produced the negative CMD5 results of reports 180-192
(traps 116-137).  It is kept as the reference for the 1917-truth re-derivation;
do not re-apply it on the "fresh derivation" path without a reason.
